# cytokine — the arms race (pathogens promoted from held dose to living population)
#
# the single-cell-to-population upgrade: pathogens is now a real `node`. it
# replicates (a flow INTO it that reads itself = exponential growth) and is
# killed by the response. the causation that cytokine.strombild only *recorded*
# now goes LIVE: load drives cytokines, cytokines drive killing, killing knocks
# load back down.
#
# killing SATURATES (hill): the innate response has a finite capacity, so a big
# enough infection outruns it. that gives a tipping point, just like the cafe —
#   small dose  (init <= ~13)  -> cleared      (pathogens -> 0)
#   large dose  (init >= ~14)  -> overwhelmed  (pathogens pinned at the cap)
# one model, two fates, set by the initial dose. flip init across the edge to flip
# the outcome (knifeEdge(model, "pathogens") names the line, as in the cafe/debt).
node pathogens : range(0, 3000), init(10)  @ bucket(fill = dots)
node cytokines : range(0, 50),   init(0)   @ bucket
external broth                                       # nutrients the infection grows on
external plasma                                      # source of cytokine protein
external cleared                                     # cytokine wash-out
external killed                                      # dead pathogens

broth     -> pathogens : proportional(of = pathogens, k = 0.15)        # replication
plasma    -> cytokines : proportional(of = pathogens, k = 0.3)         # response tracks load
cytokines -> cleared   : proportional(of = cytokines, k = 0.3)         # clearance
pathogens -> killed    : hill(of = cytokines, max = 4, k = 10, n = 1)  # killing, saturating

pathway infection : broth->pathogens, plasma->cytokines, cytokines->cleared, pathogens->killed
